## ✅ Your Slack Channel Description Viewer is ready!

Here's what was built — **`channel_description.py`** — a simple on-demand tool that fetches and displays a Slack channel's description.

### How to use it

**List available channels:**
```bash
python channel_description.py --list
```

**Look up a specific channel:**
```bash
python channel_description.py --channel general
# or with the # prefix — both work:
python channel_description.py --channel "#engineering"
```

**Interactive mode (it'll ask you):**
```bash
python channel_description.py
```

### Two modes

| Mode | When it's used | What happens |
|---|---|---|
| **Simulated** | No `SLACK_TOKEN` set (right now) | Uses built-in demo channels — great for testing |
| **Real Slack** | You set `SLACK_TOKEN=xoxb-...` | Talks to your actual Slack workspace |

### To connect to your real Slack workspace
1. Go to [api.slack.com/apps](https://api.slack.com/apps) and create an app (or use an existing one)
2. Add the `channels:read` permission scope
3. Install it to your workspace and copy the **Bot Token** (starts with `xoxb-`)
4. Run: `SLACK_TOKEN=xoxb-your-token-here python channel_description.py`

That's it! Just run it any time you want to check a channel description — no fuss, fully on demand. 🎉

